# ForenSweep Project Rules

- This repository is a Bun + Turborepo monorepo.
- Preserve existing workspace conventions and package names.
- Use TypeScript strict mode.
- Never replace Bun with npm, pnpm, or yarn.
- Backend is Node.js + Express + TypeScript.
- Frontend is React/TypeScript.
- Prisma/PostgreSQL lives in packages/db.
- Python owns low-level forensic logic and disk-image processing.
- Node API must not directly execute dd, shred, hdparm, nvme, blkdiscard, or other raw-device commands.
- Real device erasure must remain disabled by default.
- Only safe .img files inside SAFE_IMAGE_ROOT may be handled in simulation mode.
- Never accept arbitrary filesystem paths from the frontend.
- Browser sends device IDs or server-generated upload IDs only.
- Validate HTTP payloads with Zod.
- Use shared schemas/types from packages/shared.
- Convert BigInt values to strings in API and WebSocket responses.
- Use UUIDs for jobs and job-scoped output folders.
- Do not use child_process.exec with interpolated user input.
- Keep private keys, .env files, certificates, images, recovered files, and generated PDFs out of Git.
- Run typecheck/lint/tests after each task where scripts exist.
- Do not make broad unrelated refactors.
- At the end of every task, report changed files, commands run, and remaining work.